 **Pitfalls and Edge Cases**
-*   **Exponentiation Stability:** The term $|g|^{\frac{1}{\alpha x'}}$ involves exponentiation where the exponent depends on the inverse of opacity. If $\alpha x'$ approaches zero, the exponent approaches infinity, potentially causing numerical instability or overflow if $|g| > 1$. If $|g| < 1$, the term approaches zero. Implementers should guard against division by zero or extreme values in the exponent [G].
