 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: The method adds a constant number of mathematical operations (exponentiation, multiplication, addition) per sample. It does not increase the number of ray casts or lookups compared to standard CVR, unlike methods that require additional gradient lookups or ray tracing [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: No additional memory structures are required beyond standard volume data and fragment state [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Performance**: The method is designed for interactive, in-browser rendering, balancing quality and speed [S1]. It avoids the computational cost of stochastic blending by using deterministic interpolation [S1].
-*   **Strengths**: Reduces noise in volumetric data (e.g., ultrasound) by favoring volumetric shading in noisy regions; balances local and global features [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations**: May dampen small features if volumetric shading is favored too strongly [S2, unofficial]. Numerical stability of the exponent term requires careful handling of low opacity values [G].
